dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn, how are you today?
[patient] i'm doing alright.
[doctor] good. how are you feeling?
[patient] i'm just, i'm just having some pain in my elbows, you know, my right elbow is bothering me more than my left.
[doctor] okay. and you said you've been sitting at your computer a lot at work, sitting at the computer all day?
[patient] yeah, i'm at the computer all day, so i'm not sure if it's from sitting there or if it's just because i'm older, you know, my joints are just getting older.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other joint pain?
[patient] no, just my elbows.
[doctor] okay. and what happens when you sit at the computer? do you feel like it's, it's causing the pain or is it just there?
[patient] i'm not sure, i'm not sure if it's from sitting there or if it's just because i'm older.
[doctor] okay. and do you feel like it's in both elbows or is one more than the other?
[patient] my right elbow bothers me more than my left.
[doctor] okay. and are you typing or writing at your desk?
[patient] i'm typing.
[doctor] okay. and you said your right elbow bothers you more than your left, so does that mean that your right elbow is worse?
[patient] yeah, it's just, it's just a little bit worse.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other symptoms with your elbows, like any numbness or tingling?
[patient] yeah, i get some numbness and tingling in my hands and i just shake them out to relieve it.
[doctor] okay. and when did you start noticing this?
[patient] it's been a couple of weeks now.
[doctor] okay. have you been doing anything new that you think might be causing it?
[patient] no, i haven't been doing anything different.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed it with your other joints or is it just your elbows?
[patient] just my elbows.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any gout episodes recently?
[patient] i had an episode about three months ago.
[doctor] okay. and how did that go?
[patient] it was my toe.
[doctor] okay. and how did you do?
[patient] the medicine they gave me helped a lot.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any other issues with that?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any other joint pain?
[patient] no, just my elbows.
[doctor] okay. and how about your psoriasis, have you been having any issues with that?
[patient] no, it's under control.
[doctor] okay. and are you still on the colchicine?
[patient] yes, i am.
[doctor] okay. how much are you taking?
[patient] i take it twice a day.
[doctor] twice a day?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and that's for flare-ups of your gout?
[patient] yes, for flare-ups.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. well, i'm gon na go ahead and do a physical exam on you. so i'm gon na start with your neck. your neck is supple, no lymph nodes, no swelling. let's listen to your lungs. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. let's listen to your heart. your heart is regular rate and rhythm. let's look at your abdomen. your abdomen is soft. let's look at your extremities. there is no edema to your lower extremity. let's look at your right elbow. there is some edema and inflammation of the right olecranon. there is some tenderness to palpation of the olecranon bursa. there is pain with pronation and supination. there is pain with flexion and extension of the right arm. i'm gon na order an x-ray of your right elbow. i'm gon na prescribe meloxicam 15 milligrams once a day for pain and swelling. i'm gon na continue you on the colchicine 0.6 milligrams twice a day as needed for flare-ups. i'm gon na continue the steroid cream for your psoriasis. any questions about the plan?
[patient] no, i think that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. all right, well, i'll have my nurse come in and get you checked out. thank you.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
