dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, beverly, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing well. i've been doing a lot of baking this summer, but i'm excited to be here today for my annual exam.
[doctor] excellent. so, beverly, you know, i've been looking over your records. i know that you have a history of type 2 diabetes and high blood pressure. i know you've been doing well, but i do see that your blood sugars have been a little bit up and down. can you tell me a little bit about what's been going on?
[patient] yeah, i've been working at this new bakery, and i've been eating a lot of sweets, so my blood sugars have been fluctuating.
[doctor] okay. have you been taking your medication?
[patient] yes, i have. i've been taking my metformin twice a day.
[doctor] okay. and have you missed any doses?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] good. and how's your blood pressure been?
[patient] my blood pressure has been good, even though my blood sugars have been up and down.
[doctor] okay. and have you been sleeping well?
[patient] yes, i have been sleeping well. i've been able to sleep a full 8 hours.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any thoughts of self-harm or suicidal ideations?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. excellent. let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. your neck is supple without any thyroid enlargement or lymph nodes. your lungs are clear to auscultation bilaterally. no wheezes, rales, or rhonchi. your heart has a regular rate. i do appreciate a 2 out of 6 systolic ejection fraction murmur, no gallops or rubs, no extra heart sounds, good pulses. let's look at your hemoglobin a1c, and it's elevated. so, beverly, i know you've been working at the bakery, and that's been good. i know you've been trying to improve your diet by removing some of those extra sweets. do you think you can continue to do that?
[patient] yes, i can definitely try.
[doctor] okay. i'm going to continue you on your metformin twice a day. i want you to check your fasting blood glucose levels each morning and call them in about two weeks. we'll follow up in about two months, and we'll discuss further treatment recommendations. and then for your high blood pressure, you're currently on lisinopril 10 milligrams once a day. i'm going to continue you on that as well. do you have any questions for me?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] okay. well, do you have any other questions for me?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] alright. well, it was great seeing you. take care, beverly.
[patient] thank you, doctor.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
