[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and, uh, i'm gon na touch your elbow here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and, uh, i'm gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and, uh, i'm gon na press on your elbow here. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na take a look at your elbow. so, i can see some erythema and edema here. and, uh, it's warm to the touch. and, uh, it's painful to flex and extend. and, uh, i can feel your pulse here. so, let's go ahead and look at your x-ray. so, your x-ray of your left arm does not show any evidence of elbow fracture. so, let's talk a little bit about my assessment and plan. so, i believe you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. and, uh, i'm gon na start you on meloxicam 15 milligrams once daily. i want you to use a pillow to rest your arm on. you can also ice the area. so, do you have any questions about that?
[patient] no, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. and, uh, let's talk a little bit about your epilepsy. so, it sounds like you've been doing well on keppra and you haven't had any seizures recently. so, i'm gon na continue you on keppra 500 milligrams twice a day. i'm gon na refill that for you today.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and, uh, let's talk a little bit about your depression. so, it sounds like you've been doing well with therapy. and, uh, i'm gon na start you on lexapro 10 milligrams once daily.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. and, uh, let's talk a little bit about your peptic ulcer. so, it sounds like you had an endoscopy and they found gastritis. and, uh, you've been doing well on protonix. so, i'm gon na continue you on protonix 40 milligrams once daily before meals.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions about that?
[patient] no, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. great. so, do you have any other questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
[doctor] okay. alright. well, i'm gon na go ahead and see you out. thanks for coming in today.
[patient] thanks, doctor. }}<|eot_id|>
