dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, susan, how are you?
[patient] i'm doing okay, doctor.
[doctor] good to see you. so, i know you're here for a high blood pressure check. so, what's been going on?
[patient] well, i've always struggled with high blood pressure, but it seems like it's out of control lately.
[doctor] okay. have you been monitoring it at home?
[patient] yes, i have. it's been over 150.
[doctor] okay. and what have you been doing to manage it?
[patient] i've been taking my norvasc, but it doesn't seem to be working.
[doctor] okay. have you noticed any other symptoms like headaches or chest pain?
[patient] i've had some headaches, but i'm not sure if it's from stress at work or my high blood pressure.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any shortness of breath?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. have you been feeling any chest pain?
[patient] no, none of that.
[doctor] okay. i understand that you've had a kidney transplant in the past. how are you doing with that?
[patient] it's going well. i'm taking all my immunosuppression medications.
[doctor] okay. and have you noticed any swelling in your feet or ankles?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. let me go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so, your neck is supple without any swelling. your lungs are clear. i do hear a two out of six systolic ejection murmur. your heart and lungs are normal. your extremities do not have any swelling. and i see the scar on your left flank from your kidney transplant, which looks like it's healed. so, let's go ahead and look at your blood work. your creatinine is normal. your ekg is normal. i would like to get a lipid panel and a metabolic panel. i'm gon na start you on carvedilol 25 milligrams twice a day to help bring your blood pressure down. continue to take your norvasc and all of your immunosuppression medications. and we'll follow up in a month to check your blood pressure. is that okay with you?
[patient] yes, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay, great. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, i think that's it.
[doctor] okay. alright, see you in a month. }}<|eot_id|>
