dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, ms. lee, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing okay, just a little bit of pain.
[doctor] okay, so i understand you were at a birthday party and you ran into the railing of the staircase and twisted your back. how are you feeling now?
[patient] i'm feeling pretty sore.
[doctor] mm-hmm. have you had any pain down into your legs?
[patient] no, just my back.
[doctor] okay, and does anything make the pain better or worse?
[patient] lying flat and twisting makes it worse.
[doctor] okay. have you tried any ibuprofen?
[patient] i've been taking some ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay. what kind of ibuprofen have you been taking?
[patient] just over-the-counter ibuprofen.
[doctor] okay. have you had any other problems like this before?
[patient] no, this is the first time.
[doctor] okay. so let's go ahead and go ahead and do a quick physical exam. i'm gon na check your back. i'm gon na press on your back here, and it looks like you have a good range of motion without pain. i'm gon na check your legs, and i'm gon na straighten your leg up, and that's okay. that's not painful at all. i'm gon na check your sensation, and that's okay. it feels like you have sensation in your legs. so i'm gon na take a look at your back x-ray. it looks like you had a lumbar fusion in the past. and you have hardware in your back, and that's all in good position. it looks like you have a strain in your back. i'm gon na give you a diagnosis of lumbar spine strain. so i'm gon na recommend that you take some ibuprofen 800 milligrams three times a day with food. and i want you to use ice and heat. you can use ice for the first couple of days to try to reduce the pain and swelling. and then you can switch to heat to help loosen up the muscles. if you're still having a lot of pain, we can do some physical therapy. and i want you to follow up with me as needed. how does that sound?
[patient] that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay. do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] i have anxiety.
[doctor] okay. have you been seeing a therapist for that?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. i'm gon na refer you to a therapist. i think that would be helpful. i'm gon na order some physical therapy and some physical therapy exercises for you to do at home. and i'm gon na give you a prescription for some ibuprofen. and if you're still having a lot of pain, we can do some injections. does that sound okay?
[patient] yes, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. i'm gon na have my nurse come in and get you checked out.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
