dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning how are you
[patient] good morning doctor
[doctor] hey good morning so i see that you're here for follow up for your irritable bowel syndrome or ibs what's going on for you
[patient] so i've been having a lot of abdominal pain and nausea and vomiting
[doctor] okay and when did this start
[patient] it's been going on for a while now
[doctor] okay so this is new or has this been going on for a while
[patient] it's been going on for a while
[doctor] okay and when was the last time you were in
[patient] i think i was in august
[doctor] okay and what did we do for you last time
[patient] i think you gave me bentyl
[doctor] okay and i also gave you a prescription for reglan
[patient] yeah
[doctor] okay and what did you do with that
[patient] i used it as needed for nausea
[doctor] okay and then i also told you to start a low dose fiber supplement such as citrucel daily and probiotics to help with gas and bloating and to take bentyl up to four times a day for intestinal cramping
[patient] yeah
[doctor] and i also told you to discontinue the reglan and to use zofran as needed for nausea
[patient] okay
[doctor] and i know we discussed neuromodulators like elavil and buspar but we didn't start those yet
[patient] okay
[doctor] okay so tell me a little bit more about what's been going on since then
[patient] so i've been having a lot of flares of abdominal pain and i've been taking the bentyl as needed and the citrucel and i've been trying to do the probiotics but i haven't been doing it consistently
[doctor] okay and how often are you having these flares
[patient] i would say maybe monday through thursday i'm okay but then on friday i'm having a lot of cramps and sharp pains
[doctor] okay and anything that makes it better or worse
[patient] yeah i had shrimp the other day and i had upper and lower abdominal pain and a lot of bloating
[doctor] okay and did that happen after the shrimp or was it before
[patient] it was after
[doctor] okay and what else has been going on
[patient] i had chicken alfredo and that makes me have diarrhea
[doctor] okay and does that happen every time you have chicken alfredo
[patient] pretty much yeah
[doctor] okay and any other foods that make you have diarrhea
[patient] yeah i drink two drinks when i'm out and i have a martini occasionally and i do my best to avoid heavy foods but i had fried chicken today and i didn't have any symptoms
[doctor] okay and how about sodas have you been drinking those
[patient] i stopped drinking those
[doctor] okay and that's been helpful
[patient] yeah
[doctor] okay and how about your bowel movements how often are you passing stool
[patient] i'm passing 2 to 3 formed stools a day
