dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing alright, i'm just having some issues with my breathing.
[doctor] okay, what's going on with your breathing?
[patient] i've been having some shortness of breath and i've been coughing up some blood.
[doctor] okay, have you had any fever?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] have you noticed any bleeding from your gums?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay, have you been having any shortness of breath for a long time or is this a new thing?
[patient] it's been going on for a little while.
[doctor] okay, have you noticed it with any activities or is it just when you're sitting still?
[patient] it's been happening even when i'm just sitting still.
[doctor] okay, and you said you're coughing up some blood?
[patient] yes, i've been coughing up blood.
[doctor] okay, have you had any shortness of breath in the past?
[patient] yes, i've had shortness of breath in the past.
[doctor] okay, have you been diagnosed with anything?
[patient] i've been diagnosed with diabetes and hypertension.
[doctor] okay, have you been taking any medications for those?
[patient] yes, i've been taking metformin and norvasc.
[doctor] okay, all right, well, let's go ahead and review your systems real quick. have you had any fever?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] have you noticed any bleeding from your gums?
[patient] no, i have not.
[patient] respiratory, have you noticed any shortness of breath?
[patient] yes, i have.
[patient] musculoskeletal, any knee pain?
[patient] yes, i have knee pain.
[doctor] okay, any lower extremity edema?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] any bruising?
[patient] no, i do not.
[doctor] okay, let's go ahead and take a look at your vitals. your pulse ox is 94 percent and your blood pressure is 120 over 70.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right, let's go ahead and do a quick physical exam. your neck is supple, no jvd, no carotid bruits. let's listen to your lungs. there are some rales and rhonchi more on the right, no wheezing right now. there is some diminished breath sounds on the right as well. let's listen to your heart. it's regular rate, there is a 2/6 systolic ejection murmur, unchanged from before. let's listen to your abdomen. it's soft. let's look at your extremities. there is one plus non-pitting edema on your bilateral lower extremities. no calf tenderness, no homan's sign. and let's look at your skin. there is no bruising.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right, based on your symptoms and your exam, it sounds like you might have some shortness of breath.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] it could be as simple as a pneumonia or it could be something more serious. we need to get some further testing done. i'm going to have you go to the er immediately after this appointment and i will call ahead.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm also going to order a chest x-ray, ct scan, and blood work to be done in the er. i want to make sure that we get a better understanding of what's going on.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] i'm also concerned about your diabetes. your blood sugar has not been well controlled. i'm going to order an updated a1c today. i'm going to increase your metformin to 750 milligrams twice daily.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] and for your hypertension, your blood pressure has been running low for about three weeks. i believe this could be caused by your shortness of breath. i would like to get a better understanding of the cause of your shortness of breath before pursuing further treatment for your hypertension.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] at this time, you will discontinue the use of norvasc.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] do you have any questions or concerns?
[patient] no, i think you covered everything.
[doctor] okay, great. we will have you follow up in about three weeks to just discuss your diabetes and further treatment recommendations.
[patient] okay, sounds good.
[doctor] alright, thank you, see you in three weeks.
[patient] thank you. }}<|eot_id|>
