dialogue is: {{ [doctor] good morning, how are you doing today?
[patient] good morning, doctor.
[doctor] good to see you. so, i understand that you're here for right elbow pain. can you tell me a little bit more about what's going on?
[patient] yes, my elbow has been bothering me for about 4 days now. it started hurting after i was working with the pottery wheel.
[doctor] okay, and you've been using the pottery wheel a lot lately?
[patient] yes, i've been doing a lot of pottery lately, actually, i was making a bowl for my son.
[doctor] okay, and how would you rate your pain level right now?
[patient] it's a 7 out of 10.
[doctor] okay, and is it constant or does it come and go?
[patient] it's constant. it wakes me up at night when i roll over.
[doctor] okay, and does anything help with the pain?
[patient] no, i've tried ibuprofen and ice, but it doesn't seem to help.
[doctor] okay, have you had any injuries to that elbow before?
[patient] no, not that i can remember.
[doctor] okay, so you're having a lot of pain on the medial side of your elbow, and it radiates down into your arm?
[patient] yes, that's right.
[doctor] okay, and how has this affected your activities?
[patient] i can't use the pottery wheel at all.
[doctor] okay, how about other activities?
[patient] it's hard to do anything, it's really uncomfortable.
[doctor] okay, have you noticed any swelling or bruising?
[patient] no, there's no bruising or swelling.
[doctor] okay, so you've been doing a lot of pottery and making a bowl for your son. how has that been going?
[patient] it's been going good. i've been making a lot of pottery, like i said, i was making a bowl for my son. he loves it.
[doctor] okay, and do you have a history of hypertension?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay, and how are you managing that?
[patient] i take lisinopril 10 milligrams every day and i check my blood pressure regularly. it's usually in the 110s to 130s.
[doctor] okay, and do you ever miss any doses?
[patient] no, i try to take it every day.
[doctor] okay, and do you have a history of diabetes?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay, and how are you managing that?
[patient] i take metformin 500 milligrams twice a day. sometimes i forget to take it, but i try my best.
[doctor] okay, and how have your blood sugar levels been?
[patient] they've been running from 150 to 170.
[doctor] okay, and how do you exercise?
[patient] i walk in the morning and in the evening. i walk about 1 to 2 miles a day.
[doctor] okay, and do you have a sweet tooth?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay, and what do you do for fun?
[patient] i like working with ceramics and baking cakes and cinnamon rolls for family gatherings.
[doctor] okay, so you enjoy baking and ceramics. do you have any other hobbies?
[patient] yes, i love baking and ceramics.
[doctor] okay, so let's talk a little bit about your review of systems. i know you're here for your elbow pain, but can you tell me about any other symptoms you're having?
[patient] no, nothing else.
[doctor] okay, and how about any rashes or lesions on your skin?
[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay, and any respiratory problems?
[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay, and any pain or discomfort in your heart or chest?
[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay, and any dizziness or lightheadedness?
[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay, and any problems with your vision?
[patient] no, nothing.
[doctor] okay, and any problems with your bowels?
[patient] no, nothing.
