dialogue is: {{ [doctor] Good morning, how are you today?

[patient] Good morning, I'm okay. I've been feeling a bit better since my last visit.

[doctor] That's good to hear. How has your blood pressure been since we last checked it?

[patient] It's been a bit higher, but I've been checking it regularly.

[doctor] How high has it been?

[patient] It's been averaging 135-145 over 95-110.

[doctor] I see. Have you noticed any side effects from the medications I prescribed, the lisinopril and hydrochlorothiazide?

[patient] Yes, I had some side effects. I experienced headaches, a "swooshing" in my left ear, and I felt lethargic.

[doctor] Hmm, that doesn't sound pleasant. Did you try reducing the dose of lisinopril to see if it helped?

[patient] Yes, I took half a dose and didn't experience the side effects.

[doctor] Good to know. Have you been able to cut down on your alcohol consumption?

[patient] No, I still consume it 4-5 times a week.

[doctor] I see. It's important to note that if you stopped drinking completely, your blood pressure would likely improve significantly.

[patient] I know, but it's hard for me to stop.

[doctor] I understand. Let's discuss the possibility of Naltrexone injections to help with your alcohol use disorder. Have you considered this before?

[patient] Yes, I've heard about it. I'm interested in it.

[doctor] Alright. We can start you on the injectable form of Naltrexone, which we've discussed before. It will be given to you on May 17th. We'll review the potential side effects and risks again before starting.

[patient] That sounds good.

[doctor] We'll also continue with the lisinopril 10 mg once daily and hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg once daily. Your target blood pressure is 130-140/70-80. We'll reassess your blood pressure at your next visit.

[patient] Okay, that sounds good.

[doctor] I also recommend getting your influenza vaccination and Shingrix #2. You've deferred this before, but it's important to stay up to date on your vaccinations.

[patient] I'll make sure to get it done.

[doctor] Great. We'll see you back in the clinic for your next visit in the week of June 14th, which will be the time of your second Naltrexone injection. If you have any questions or concerns, please feel free to call the clinic.

[patient] Alright, I'll do that. Thank you.

[doctor] You're welcome. Take care and see you next time.

[patient] Thank you, doctor. }}<|eot_id|>
