dialogue is: {{ [doctor]: Hi there, how are you today?

[patient]: I'm okay, I guess. I've been having a lot of pain in my right shoulder.

[doctor]: I see. Can you tell me more about this pain?

[patient]: Sure. It happened four days ago when I was playing pick-up football. I got tackled a couple of times and landed on my right shoulder.

[doctor]: Oh, I see. Did you continue playing after that?

[patient]: Yes, I did. But I've been having pain since then.

[doctor]: Where exactly do you feel the pain?

[patient]: It's mainly on the back of my shoulder.

[doctor]: Okay. Have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your fingers?

[patient]: No, I haven't.

[doctor]: That's good. How about the strength in your hand?

[patient]: It's okay, but I've been trying to avoid lifting anything heavy.

[doctor]: Hmm. Can you touch your shoulder to your ear?

[patient]: No, it hurts too much.

[doctor]: I understand. Have you been taking any medication for the pain?

[patient]: Yes, I've been taking Tylenol, but it doesn't seem to be helping much.

[doctor]: Alright. Have you had any neck problems or other joint problems in the past?

[patient]: No, I haven't.

[doctor]: Okay. Did you hit your head during the injury?

[patient]: Yes, I did, but I didn't pass out.

[doctor]: That's good. Have you had any fever or chills since the injury?

[patient]: No, I haven't.

[doctor]: Alright. Let's go over your medical history. Have you had any previous surgeries?

[patient]: Yes, I had an appendectomy about three to four years ago.

[doctor]: Okay. Have you noticed any other symptoms such as fever or chills?

[patient]: No, nothing like that.

[doctor]: Alright. Let's do a quick review of your systems. How about your overall health?

[patient]: I feel fine, no fever or chills.

[doctor]: Good. How about your muscles and joints?

[patient]: I have pain in my right shoulder.

[doctor]: And any neurological symptoms?

[patient]: I've had a headache, but no numbness or tingling.

[doctor]: Okay. Let's check your vital signs. Your blood pressure is 122/76, heart rate is 82 bpm, and your oxygen saturation is 95% on room air. Everything looks good there.

[patient]: That sounds good.

[doctor]: Now, let's do a physical exam. I'll start with your neck. Is there any tenderness when I press on it?

[patient]: No, it doesn't hurt.

[doctor]: Good. How about your head? Any trauma or bruising?

[patient]: No, there's nothing like that.

[doctor]: Alright. Now, let's examine your shoulder. I'll check for any pain or tenderness. Hmm, I can feel some pain when I press on the back of your shoulder, specifically at the acromioclavicular joint.

[patient]: That's where I've been feeling the pain.

[doctor]: I see. Can you move your arm for me? How about abduction and adduction?

[patient]: It hurts when I move it. I can only move it to about 90 degrees.

[doctor]: Okay. What about supination and pronation?

[patient]: That hurts too.

[doctor]: Alright. I can feel your radial artery pulse. It's normal. Let's get some X-rays of your shoulder to take a closer look.

[patient]: Okay.

[doctor]: The X-rays show an acute acromioclavicular joint fracture.

[patient]: Oh no, that doesn't sound good.

[doctor]: It's not too serious, but we need to take care of it. I'm going to put you in a sling to immobilize your shoulder and prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day to help with the pain.

[patient]: Okay, that sounds good.

[doctor]: I also recommend a CT scan of your shoulder to evaluate further. We'll get you scheduled for that soon.

[patient]: Alright, I'll do that.

[doctor]: Additionally, I advise you to avoid tackle football for now and attend formal physical therapy to strengthen your shoulder. This will help prevent surgery in the future.

[patient]: I'll definitely avoid football and start physical therapy.

[doctor]: Great. Do you have any questions or concerns?

[patient]: No, I think that covers everything.

[doctor]: Alright, I'll see you in a few days to follow up on your progress. We'll review the CT scan results then.

[patient]: Sounds good. Thanks for everything.

[doctor]: You're welcome. Take care and see you soon. }}<|eot_id|>
