dialogue is: {{ [doctor] Good morning, how are you today?

[patient] Good morning, I'm doing alright, thanks. I've been having some issues with my right knee.

[doctor] I see. What seems to be going on with your knee?

[patient] Well, about two and a half weeks ago, I stepped off a curb and twisted my ankle. It's been hurting ever since.

[doctor] Hmm, I see. Where exactly do you feel the pain?

[patient] It's on the outside of my right knee.

[doctor] Does it hurt when you walk?

[patient] No, it doesn't. Unless I stand on one foot for a long time. Then it starts to hurt.

[doctor] Okay, and do you feel any pain when you stand with both feet flat on the ground?

[patient] No, it's only when I'm on one foot.

[doctor] How about when you're resting and elevating your leg? Does it hurt then?

[patient] No, it doesn't.

[doctor] And what about when you're sitting or lying down? Does it hurt then?

[patient] No, it's only when I'm standing or standing on one foot.

[doctor] Alright, that's helpful. Do you notice any clicking or locking of your knee when you move it?

[patient] Yes, I do feel some clicking when I walk.

[doctor] How about when you rest your foot on your heel? Does it hurt then?

[patient] Yes, it does.

[doctor] Have you noticed any numbness or tingling in your right foot?

[patient] Yes, I have numbness and tingling in my toes, but that's not new. It's been there for a while.

[doctor] Okay, I see. Have you been doing anything to manage the pain?

[patient] I've been taking ibuprofen and icing my knee four times a day. It helps a bit.

[doctor] That's good. How much relief do you get from the ibuprofen and icing?

[patient] It gives me relief at night and in the morning, but it doesn't last all day.

[doctor] Alright. Have you noticed any impact on your daily activities due to the pain?

[patient] No, I'm still pretty active during the day, but it doesn't affect me too much.

[doctor] Okay, have you been able to do any full squats without pain?

[patient] Yes, I can do a full squat without pain.

[doctor] That's good to hear. Have you had any other medical issues or surgeries?

[patient] I've fractured my second toe three times in the last 10 years.

[doctor] Okay. Do you have any other medical conditions or allergies I should know about?

[patient] No, none that I'm aware of.

[doctor] Great. What do you do for a living?

[patient] I work in sales.

[doctor] Okay. Do you have any hobbies or exercise routines?

[patient] I like to ride my bike for exercise.

[doctor] Alright. Let's do a quick physical examination. Can you stand up for me?

[patient] Sure.

[doctor] Can you lift your foot off the ground and let me check your ankle?

[patient] Okay.

[doctor] Everything looks good there. Now, can you let me check your knee?

[patient] Sure.

[doctor] Can you straighten your knee for me?

[patient] Yes.

[doctor] And now, can you bend it?

[patient] Yes.

[doctor] I see some slight swelling and a slight fluid accumulation in your knee. Does it hurt when I press on the outside of your knee?

[patient] No, it doesn't hurt.

[doctor] That's good. Can you stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and I'll check the stability of your knee?

[patient] Sure.

[doctor] Okay, I'm going to push your knee in. Does it hurt?

[patient] No, it doesn't.

[doctor] Alright, let's take a look at your X-rays. Everything looks normal, no fractures or dislocations. I'm going to order an MRI if the pain doesn't improve with physical therapy.

[patient] Okay, what's the plan?

[doctor] I'm going to prescribe meloxicam 15 mg to help with the pain. I also recommend you start formal physical therapy to strengthen your right knee. This will help with your pain and improve your knee function. If the pain doesn't improve with physical therapy, we'll consider the MRI.

[patient] Alright, I'll do that.

[doctor] Great. Do you have any questions or concerns?

[patient] No, that sounds good. Thank you.

[doctor] You're welcome. I'll get the prescription ready for you. Do you have any insurance or identification with you?

[patient] Yes, I have my insurance card and ID.

[doctor] Great. I'll get the prescription filled and you can pick it up at the pharmacy. You can start physical therapy as soon as you like. If you have any questions or concerns, feel free to call the clinic.

[patient] Thank you, I will.

[doctor] You're welcome. Take care and see you soon.

[patient] Thank you, you too.

[doctor] Bye.

[patient] Bye. }}<|eot_id|>
