dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, carolyn. how are you doing today?
[patient] i'm doing good. i'm doing good.
[doctor] all right. so i know you're here today for a followup of your chronic problem. is everything okay?
[patient] yeah, i'm doing okay. i'm just having a little bit of flare up of my arthritis. it's been bothering me a little bit more in my elbows.
[doctor] okay. so, is it just in your elbows or is it elsewhere?
[patient] just in my elbows.
[doctor] okay. so, which elbow is it?
[patient] the right one.
[doctor] okay. so, is it just the right one or is it the left one as well?
[patient] it's more the right one.
[doctor] okay. so, is there any particular position that you're sitting in that makes it worse?
[patient] i'm sitting at the computer all day, so i'm not sure if it's just from sitting there or if it's just from typing.
[doctor] okay. so, you're typing all day?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. and are you writing as well?
[patient] i'm writing, but mostly typing.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other joint pain?
[patient] no, just my elbows.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any numbness or tingling in your hands?
[patient] yeah, sometimes.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any problems with your hands?
[patient] no, i just shake them out.
[doctor] okay. so, you shake them out and it goes away?
[patient] yeah.
[doctor] okay. and when did you have your last gout episode?
[patient] about three months ago.
[doctor] okay. and what happened?
[patient] i had some inflammation of my toe.
[doctor] okay. and did we treat you with anything?
[patient] i think i was given some medicine.
[doctor] okay. and what was the medicine?
[patient] i don't remember. i think it was some kind of steroid.
[doctor] okay. and did it help?
[patient] it did.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any problems since then?
[patient] no, not that i've noticed.
[doctor] okay. and what about your psoriasis?
[patient] it's under control. i haven't had any problems with that.
[doctor] okay. and do you have to use any creams or anything?
[patient] i use some steroid cream.
[doctor] okay. and how often do you use that?
[patient] i use it as needed.
[doctor] okay. all right. so, let's do a quick physical exam. so, your vital signs look good. your heart and lungs are clear. your abdomen is soft. your neck is supple without any lymph nodes. and on your musculoskeletal exam, your lower extremities are okay. there is some edema and inflammation of your right olecranon. there is some tenderness to palpation of your olecranon bursa. there is some pain with pronation and supination. there is some pain with flexion and extension of your right arm.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, let's talk a little bit about your medical treatment plan. so, for your gout, we'll continue the colchicine 0.6 mg twice a day as needed for flare-ups. for your osteoarthritis, we'll order an x-ray of your right elbow. and we'll prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day for pain and swelling. and for your psoriasis, we'll continue the steroid cream. do you have any questions?
[patient] no, that sounds good.
[doctor] okay. do you have any other questions?
[patient] no, that's it.
[doctor] okay. all right. well, we'll get the x-ray ordered today and we'll call you in about a week to check on you and get the results. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] all right. we'll see you then.
[patient] okay. thank you.
[doctor] you're welcome. }}<|eot_id|>
