dialogue is: {{ [doctor] hi, brittany. it's good to see you. how are you doing?
[patient] i'm doing okay. i'm just having some stomach issues.
[doctor] okay. so, i'm gon na go ahead and review your vitals. your blood pressure is a little bit high, but that's okay. it's not concerning for today. i'm gon na go ahead and review your symptoms. so, you're having some stomach issues. you're having some nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain. and when was this started?
[patient] um, i think it started about a week ago.
[doctor] okay. and have you had this before?
[patient] yeah, i have. i've had it a lot in the past, but it seems to be getting worse.
[doctor] okay. and, um, what makes it better? what makes it worse?
[patient] um, i think it's just stress. i think it's just stress. and, um, i think i might be eating some bad foods, but i don't know.
[doctor] okay. and, um, what kind of foods are you eating?
[patient] i don't know. i just eat a lot of greasy foods, i guess. and, um, i have been drinking a lot of soda, which i know i shouldn't be. i've been trying to cut back on that, but it's hard.
[doctor] okay. and, um, what kind of greasy foods?
[patient] um, like fried chicken. i love fried chicken.
[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any other symptoms?
[patient] i have some diarrhea, and i have some abdominal pain. and i feel really bloated.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any other symptoms?
[patient] no, that's it. i've been feeling really nauseous.
[doctor] okay. and, um, what have you been eating that makes you nauseous?
[patient] um, i think it's the fried chicken. i just ate fried chicken today, and it made me really sick.
[doctor] okay. and, um, how many times a day do you eat?
[patient] i eat like three times a day.
[doctor] okay. and, um, do you drink a lot of fluids?
[patient] yeah, i drink a lot of fluids. i drink soda. i drink water. i drink juice.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any blood in your stool?
[patient] no, i have not.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you noticed any weight loss?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and, um, how are you sleeping at night?
[patient] i'm not sleeping very well. i'm having a lot of trouble sleeping.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been having any stress?
[patient] i've been having a lot of stress. i've been working a lot. i've been going to school. i've been trying to do a lot of things.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been feeling stressed for a long time?
[patient] yeah, i've been feeling stressed for a long time. it's just been really bad lately.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you tried any stress relief techniques?
[patient] um, i've been trying to take some deep breaths. i've been trying to relax. i've been trying to take some baths. i've been trying to do some yoga.
[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. and, um, do you have any allergies to any medications?
[patient] no, i don't think so.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you taken any medications in the past?
[patient] no, i haven't.
[doctor] okay. and, um, have you been to the emergency room for this?
[patient] no, i haven't. i've been trying to avoid going.
[doctor] okay. well, i'm gon na go ahead and examine you. and, um, everything looks good. your abdomen is soft, non-tender. you do have some gas and bloating, but your bowels are moving well. and, um, your lungs are clear. your heart is regular. so, um, i'm gon na go ahead and tell you what i think is going on. i think you have irritable bowel syndrome. and it's something that we can treat. and i'm gon na tell you what i think we should do for it.
[patient] okay.
[doctor] so, um, i'm gon na start you on a low dose fiber supplement. i'm gon na start you on some probiotics to help with the gas and the bloating. and i'm gon na start you on some bentyl. and i want you to take that 20 milligrams as needed for your abdominal pain. i want you to take it 30 to 45 minutes before you eat out at a restaurant. and i want you to take zofran as needed for your nausea. and i want you to reduce your greasy foods. i want you to reduce your fried chicken and your soda. i want you to drink more water and i want you to try to avoid heavy foods. and i want you to try to take a low dose of elavil at night. that's a medication that can help with your anxiety and your depression. and, um, i want you to take that 25 milligrams at night. i want you to take it before you go to bed. and, um, i want you to come back and see me in a month. i want you to send me a message on your mychart if you have any side effects or if you need to adjust your medication. okay?
[patient] okay.
[doctor] alright. any questions?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. alright. i'll see you in a month. }}<|eot_id|>
