dialogue is: {{ [doctor] dennis martin is a pleasant 46-year-old male who presents to the clinic today for the evaluation of right heel pain. he's here for the evaluation of right heel pain. so dennis, i know that you've been training for a triathlon. when did your pain start?
[patient] it started about ten days ago.
[doctor] okay. and can you tell me where it is?
[patient] it's on the back of my heel.
[doctor] okay. and does it go anywhere else?
[patient] it kind of goes up into my calf.
[doctor] okay. and is it worse at any particular time of the day?
[patient] yeah, it's worse when i first get up in the morning and when i'm working out.
[doctor] okay. and if you sit for a long time, does it come back?
[patient] it does.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any pain in your left leg?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. and what kind of exercises do you do?
[patient] i run 10 kilometers in the morning. and then at lunch, i try to get on a bike for about 45 minutes to an hour. and then in the evening, i go to the aquatic center and i swim for 30 minutes to an hour. so i run 5 days a week. and then i alternate between a long run and a long bike ride on the weekends. i take one day off from my exercises.
[doctor] okay. and do you stretch at all?
[patient] no, i don't.
[doctor] okay. so i'm gon na go ahead and do a quick physical exam. so i'm gon na go ahead and press on your right heel. and i'm gon na press on your left heel. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and then i'm gon na press on the bottom of your right heel. and i'm gon na press on the bottom of your left heel. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. and then i'm gon na bend your right foot up and down. and i'm gon na bend your left foot up and down. do you feel any pain?
[patient] yes, i do.
[doctor] okay. and then i'm gon na push on your calf. and i'm gon na push on your other calf. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. so i'm gon na go ahead and squeeze the back of your heel. and i'm gon na squeeze the back of your other heel. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. so let me go ahead and take a look at your heel. so i'm gon na push on your heel. and i'm gon na push on your other heel. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. so i'm gon na go ahead and take a look at your calf. and i'm gon na push on your calf. and i'm gon na push on your other calf. does that hurt?
[patient] yes, it does.
[doctor] okay. so based on my physical exam, i think that you have a right achilles tendinitis. so i'm gon na go ahead and prescribe you some ibuprofen. i'm gon na give you three tablets of ibuprofen to take every six hours for the pain. and i'm gon na give you a referral to see a physical therapist. i want you to take at least a week off from your training. and if your pain does not improve with the physical therapy, i'm gon na recommend getting an x-ray. i'm gon na give you a script for that. and then i want you to follow up with me in seven to ten days to check on your progress. does that make sense?
[patient] yes, that does.
[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
