[patient] about a year.
[doctor] okay. and how did it start?
[patient] i just got a blister and it just wouldn't heal.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any pain with it?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and have you been wearing your regular shoes?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and have you been able to walk on it?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and when did you last see your primary care physician?
[patient] about five months ago.
[doctor] okay. and what did she give you?
[patient] keflex.
[doctor] okay. and did that help?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and when did you stop the keflex?
[patient] about five months ago.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any pain?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any drainage?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any fatigue?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and have you had any decreased sensation in your foot?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. and do you have diabetes?
[patient] yes.
[doctor] okay. what kind of diabetes do you have?
[patient] type two.
[doctor] okay. and are you taking any medication for your diabetes?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and what's your last hemoglobin a one c?
[patient] ten.
[doctor] okay. and what's your blood sugars been running?
[patient] they're running a little better than they were.
[doctor] okay. and how are they running?
[patient] they're still in the two hundreds.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other medical problems?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and do you have any other symptoms?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and when was your last hemoglobin a one c?
[patient] five months ago.
[doctor] okay. and what was your last hemoglobin a one c?
[patient] ten.
[doctor] okay. so let's take a look at your foot. so i'm just gon na look at your foot here. and i do see a one centimeter by two centimeter wound on the dorsal aspect of the lateral right foot just proximal to the five mtp joint. and i do see some yellow slough that is present with minimal granulation tissue. there is no surrounding erythema or cellulitis. there is no evidence of fluid collection. i do not see necrosis. there is no odor. and i do not appreciate any bony exposure. and i do not appreciate any pain to palpation. do you have any pain?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. and i'm gon na do an x-ray of your right foot today. and it does not show any evidence of osteomyelitis. so i'm gon na go ahead and do a debridement in the office today. and i'm gon na put you in a surgical shoe to provide increased support. i'm gon na prescribe you collagenase ointment to apply to your wound one time per day and cover it with a sterile dressing. and i want you to continue this until we see your ulcer decrease in size. and i'm gon na order an ankle brachial index to determine your blood supply to see if we can heal your wound. and i want you to follow up with me in two weeks to check on your progress. any questions?
[patient] no.
[doctor] okay. }}<|eot_id|>
